Manifest zones are geographic areas where the boundary between [[Eberron]] and one of the Outer Planes (or [[Khyber]]/[[Siberys]]) is thin. They create localized magical effects that can be either beneficial or hazardous.

!! How They Work
The thirteen planes of the Eberron cosmology move through periods of coterminous (close) and remote (distant) alignment. In a manifest zone, the associated plane's influence is always present regardless of the current alignment cycle.

!! Notable Manifest Zones
|Location|Plane|Effect|
|[[Sharn]]|Syrania (Azure Sky)|Empowers flight and levitation; allows Sharn's impossible tower heights|
|[[Thelanis Crossings]]|Thelanis (Faerie)|Fey intrusions, enchantment amplification|
|[[Dreadhold]]|Dolurrh (Realm of the Dead)|Suppresses resurrection magic; used deliberately for the prison|
|[[The Mournland]] (contested)|Mabar (Endless Night)|Wounds don't heal; light is dimmed; undead are strengthened|
|[[Manifest, Aundair]]|Fernia (Sea of Fire)|Pyromantic amplification; extreme heat|

!! Game Mechanics
In a manifest zone:
* Spells of the associated plane's domain are heightened (cast at +1 level)
* Opposed spells may be suppressed or require concentration checks
* Some zones grant passive environmental effects (flight in Sharn, no healing in Mournland)
* Portals to the associated plane may be opened more easily

